// Interior recipes (DEC-088, DEC-098 §4): what a place's room is like when
// the player walks in. Presentation data: the client composes the room from
// a recipe and a keyed seed (DEC-085's rules, applied to rooms); the engine
// validates the recipes here and never reads them, so they cannot change a
// simulation result. Types: `mandate-content/src/interiors.rs`. A place kind
// names its recipe in places.jsonc (`"interior": "interior.diner"`); a kind
// without one keeps the place panel. The composer and the parts it draws
// with (part ids, surfaces, ramps) are the art pack's, in tools/pixelkit
// (`art/mandate/interiors*.ts`), which reads this file.
//
// Coordinates are floor tiles (16 px): (0, 0) is the tile under the back
// wall's left end, x to the right, y toward the viewer; the entrance is in
// the front wall at (`door`, rows - 1). Wall parts take a column and the
// height of their centre on the wall face (`wy`, px from its top), or stand
// on the floor line (`floor`); `front` parts sit on the front wall's top.
// `version`: a change that moves anything for the same seed bumps it.
//
// - `pieces`: parts on floor tiles (`x`, `y`, `len` for strips, `mirror`,
//   px nudges `dx`/`dy`), alternatives the seed picks between, a `chance`.
// - `patches`: another floor surface, a rug or a dais.
// - `choices`: arrangements the seed picks between; each option brings its
//   own pieces, patches, spots and hotspots.
// - `spots`: where the people present stand or sit, by role, in order.
// - `cast`: how the engine's place view says someone is here (`here_as`:
//   presiding, member, works, visitor) → the spot roles they take, in order
//   of preference. Nobody is placed by office or name (DEC-098).
// - `extras`: staff roles drawn as scenery when no one present takes them
//   (the clerk behind the counter, the cook), like the street's townsfolk:
//   no name tag, no conversation.
// - `hotspots`: a rectangle of tiles, the actions and services offered there
//   (from this place kind's `actions`, `late_night` and `services`), and the
//   tile the player stands on to use them; `late` ones only late at night.
//
// `content validate` checks the tile rules (parts known to the art pack,
// footprints inside the room and apart, wall parts on the wall face, every
// spot and stand on walkable floor reachable from the door, sitters on
// seats, stands next to their hotspot) for every option combination, and
// that every hotspot's actions and services are this place kind's.
{
  "kind": "interiors",
  "items": [
    // The council chamber: formal. A dais with the chair's seat under the
    // crest, the clerk's table before it, members' desks as a horseshoe or
    // in rows, a lectern, a balustrade and two rows of pews for the public.
